TROE shared data
================

/share contains immutable, architecture-independent data shipped with TROE.
Each producer owns a directory named /share/<producer> so examples, templates,
schemas, themes, and similar assets remain easy to find and cannot collide.

Executables belong in /bin and persistent or mounted data in /vol. KEX
applications are statically linked, so /lib is absent. Recovery-only bootstrap
files live under /recovery. The package-managed namespace uses writable desired configuration
in /config and exposes the active generation's resolved, non-secret
configuration read-only in /sys/config; /etc is absent and is not an alias.

/share/lua/examples contains three runnable tours: language.lua covers core
language and library features, numbers.lua covers deterministic arithmetic and
random sampling, and system.lua covers TROE filesystem, process, module, and
environment integration.

/share/lua/benchmark.lua is a portable Lua 5.5 compute and allocation
benchmark. Run the same file and arguments under TROE's `lua` and Alpine's
`lua5.5` to compare interpreter throughput and Lua-managed heap behavior.
Its `collectgarbage("count")` fields describe Lua's heap, not whole-process or
whole-system memory.
